#: miniworlds_data.stepper.Stepper:1 of
msgid "Drives a generator-based algorithm one visible step per frame."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds_data.stepper.Stepper:3 of
msgid ""
"Classical algorithms written as loops run entirely within a single frame,"
" so their intermediate states are never visible. ``Stepper`` solves this "
"by letting the algorithm be written as a *generator* that yields once per"
" step; the stepper advances it frame by frame (or on demand)."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds_data.stepper.Stepper:8 of
msgid ""
"Each yielded step is a ``(name, payload)`` tuple (see :data:`Step`). The "
"stepper records every step so it can replay them forward and backward. "
"For backward stepping (``prev_step``, ``reset``, ``goto``) you must pass "
"an ``on_reset`` callback that restores the visualization to its initial "
"state, since algorithm steps like \"swap\" are not idempotent."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds_data.stepper.Stepper:15 of
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds_data.stepper.Stepper.auto_advance:1 of
msgid "Whether the stepper advances automatically each frame."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds_data.stepper.Stepper.finished:1 of
msgid "``True`` once the generator has been exhausted."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds_data.stepper.Stepper.goto:1 of
msgid "Move to an absolute step index."
msgstr ""

#: miniworlds_data.stepper.Stepper.goto:3 of
msgid ""
"A negative index rewinds to the start; an index past the end advances as "
"far as the generator allows. Backward jumps require ``on_reset``."
msgstr ""

